    "body": ">I don't know what's going on with the keyframes case; too much prose.\r\n\r\n```webidl\r\ndictionary Keyframe {\r\n    // ... property-value pairs ...\r\n    // i.e. DOMString propertyName\r\n    double?             offset = null;\r\n    DOMString           easing = \"linear\";\r\n    CompositeOperation  composite;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// This constructor receives `sequence<Keyframe>`, but specced as `object`\r\nnew SharedKeyframeList([\r\n  { transform: 'translateY(0px)' }, // a key-value pair not specced in Keyframe, but has a meaning\r\n  { transform: 'translateY(-300px)' }\r\n]);\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe spec's algorithm gets the ES object, run [the ES-to-dictionary conversion](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#es-to-dictionary) explicitly, and then again [extracts remaining fields](https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations/#idl-attribute-name-to-animation-property-name) from the original object.",
